// spec: a lambda's capture by name of a `when` local (design.md 19) is a use of it, checked in the configuration being built: where the local does not exist (tracing is off here), the capture is an error at the lambda, never a capture of an outer or library name of that spelling
// factorio: none: the converter writes each use of a debug-only local inside `if constexpr (config::debug)` or `when (config::debug)`
// kpp: --config tracing=false
// error: when_capture_outside_its_condition_is_error.kpp:9: error: 'count' exists only when config::tracing holds: use it inside `if constexpr (config::tracing)` or a `when` on it
int main()
{
  when (config::tracing) int count = 3;
  int total = 1;
  auto read = [count]() { return 0; };
  total += read();
  println(total);
  return 0;
}
